course: dictionary
lesson: 5724
title: Loosen: making things less tight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Loosen is a verb. It means to make something less tight, firm or fixed. You loosen a belt, a knot or a screw when you make it less tight. «Loosen your belt» tells you to make the belt less tight around your middle.
explain: Loosen can also mean to become less tight by itself. «A stuck jar lid loosens under the hot tap.» The lid was too tight, and the heat makes it less tight, so it turns more easily.
explain: The word can even describe rules and control. To loosen rules is to make them less strict. Context helps you spot the meaning: look at what is being loosened, such as a knot, a grip, a belt or a rule, and ask whether it could be tight or strict.
fact: Loosen means to make something less tight, firm or fixed.
fact: «Loosen a knot» means to undo some of its tightness so it is easier to open.
fact: «Loosen up» is a phrase that means to relax.
fact: You loosen a screw by turning it anticlockwise.
fact: Loosen can mean making rules or control less strict.
exercise: «Soap loosens dirt and germs so that water can rinse them away.» What does loosens mean here? | Hides the dirt under a layer of foam | *Makes dirt and germs less stuck, so water can rinse them away | Makes dirt and germs stronger and harder to remove | Turns the dirt into water
exercise: «A stuck jar lid loosens under the hot tap.» What is happening to the lid? | *It becomes less tight, so it turns more easily | It melts and falls off the jar | It becomes tighter and harder to open | It gets bigger and cracks the glass
exercise: Find and copy the word from «loosen your belt» that tells you what to do to the belt. | to | *loosen | your | belt
test: Nadia says «loosen up» means to get tighter and stricter. What does loosen up really mean? | To fall over | *To relax | To get tighter and stricter | To shout loudly
test: «The teacher decided to loosen the rules on the trip.» What does loosen the rules mean? | Write the rules down again | Throw the rules away | *Make the rules less strict | Make the rules more strict
exam: You want to loosen a screw. Which way do you turn the screwdriver? | Gently tap it with a hammer | Clockwise | Upside down | *Anticlockwise
